WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:07.900
In your first interview, you talked about having a lot of family living by . . . living around you.

2
00:00:07.900 --> 00:00:12.620
What was it like to have . . . growing up with so many relatives nearby?

3
00:00:12.620 --> 00:00:14.800
It was amazing.

4
00:00:14.800 --> 00:00:17.900
I just . . . It’s hard to identify, I mean,

5
00:00:17.900 --> 00:00:28.980
now with families having kids and stuff that stay all over the country . . . aunts and uncles . . . because most of mine,

6
00:00:28.980 --> 00:00:32.760
particularly on my mother’s side of the family,

7
00:00:32.760 --> 00:00:43.000
they basically all lived in a circle around our house and not more than . . . None of them lived more than 300 yards away.

8
00:00:43.000 --> 00:00:45.900
It was a large family, her sisters and brothers.

9
00:00:45.900 --> 00:00:52.240
And on my father’s side of the family, the Braxton side of the family, there were . . . Well,

10
00:00:52.240 --> 00:01:05.760
a whole subdivision was named after the Braxtons. [Laughs] It was Braxtons all over the place that were relatives.

11
00:01:05.760 --> 00:01:13.020
All but about two of my uncles that were living during the time I was coming up,

12
00:01:13.020 --> 00:01:18.340
all but two lived in the area of Mossville . . . lived in Mossville.

13
00:01:18.340 --> 00:01:23.920
So it was very close family situation.

14
00:01:23.920 --> 00:01:26.020
Everybody was around.

15
00:01:26.020 --> 00:01:31.800
Practically, at one time I think the population of Mossville exceeded two thousand people,

16
00:01:31.800 --> 00:01:37.840
and the greater majority of those was related to me some way, somehow.

17
00:01:37.840 --> 00:01:44.780
One thing about it as it connects to Mossville was that practically everybody was kin.

18
00:01:44.780 --> 00:01:46.240
I mean, they carried the last name.

19
00:01:46.240 --> 00:01:52.340
Moss, Mossville was named after some Mosses . . . Mossville.

20
00:01:52.340 --> 00:02:00.315
I’m not so sure that it picks up the name because the Mosses was the first . . . most prominent settlers here,

21
00:02:00.315 --> 00:02:04.840
or if it was just that Moss had the first post office here.

22
00:02:04.840 --> 00:02:10.760
And when you get a post office, you have to have a town designation to go with it.
